[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2733664638","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/103922#issuecomment-2733664638","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103922","id":2733664638,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6i8Gl-","user":{"login":"KoBeWi","id":2223172,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyMjMxNzI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2223172?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi","html_url":"https://github.com/KoBeWi","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-18T15:25:05Z","updated_at":"2025-03-19T21:23:46Z","body":"Changing Control's `theme` should update property list, because the variations require re-selecting the node to appear.\r\nAlso if you assign a theme, it will override the variation list from project's/default theme. The lists should be merged instead.\r\n\r\nI think the fix is fine overall. Ideally the Control should fetch variations from all Themes in parent Control nodes (so e.g. if you have 3 nested Controls, each with a theme, the variations should be fetched and combined from all themes). **That** could be performance-intensive though, so your solution, while it's not complete, is better than the current state.\r\n\r\nEDIT:\r\nFor the property list update, you can use NOTIFICATION_THEME_CHANGED.",